---
// The Chrome Web Store requires a reachable privacy policy URL for any
// extension that handles authentication information — Tiro Clipper stores a
// GitHub token. Bilingual on purpose: the site reads Chinese, store reviewers
// read English.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "2026-08-28";
---

<Base title="隐私政策">
  <article
    class="prose prose-neutral mx-auto max-w-3xl dark:prose-invert prose-headings:font-bold"
  >
    <h1>隐私政策 / Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500">最后更新 / Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>中文</h2>

    <p>
      Tiro 由两部分组成：Chrome 扩展 <strong>Tiro Clipper</strong>，以及本站点。
      两者都不设置追踪 Cookie，不接入任何分析或广告服务，也不出售你的数据。
      扩展只把数据发往一个第三方：GitHub——发到你自己指定的仓库，用你自己的令牌，
      且只在你按下「剪藏」之后。
    </p>

    <h3>扩展存储什么</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        你在设置页填写的 GitHub
        用户名、仓库名、分支名，以及个人访问令牌（PAT）。
      </li>
      <li>
        这些内容保存在本机的 <code>chrome.storage.local</code> 中，不会同步到其他设备，
        也不会上传到除 GitHub 以外的任何服务器。
      </li>
      <li>以及一条记录：你在哪一刻同意了首次弹出的数据说明。</li>
      <li>你的界面语言选择（自动 / English / 中文）。</li>
      <li>
        还有一份本机的剪藏记录：每次成功剪藏后，记下该页面地址对应的标识
        （slug）和时间，用于下次打开弹窗时提示「已剪藏过」。这份记录同样只存在
        <code>chrome.storage.local</code> 中（最多保留 500 条）， 不会发送到任何地方。
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>扩展何时读取页面</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        在某个页面上点击工具栏里的 Tiro 图标、打开弹窗时，扩展就会读取该页面，
        用于生成预览（标题、字数）。<strong>这发生在你点击「剪藏」之前</strong
        >。
      </li>
      <li>
        首次使用时，弹窗会先显示一段数据说明，只有你确认之后才会读取页面。
      </li>
      <li>
        读取结果只留在浏览器里。若你不点「剪藏」就关闭弹窗，结果随即丢弃，
        不会发送、也不会保存。
      </li>
      <li>
        扩展不会在后台浏览、读取或上传任何页面；没打开弹窗的页面它碰不到。
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>扩展发送什么、发到哪里</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        唯一的网络目标是 <code>https://api.github.com</code>，这也是扩展在
        <code>host_permissions</code> 中申请的唯一域名。
      </li>
      <li>
        点击「剪藏」后，扩展用你自己的令牌把这些内容提交到你自己的仓库：正文的
        Markdown、标题、原文网址、域名和剪藏时间。标题还会出现在提交信息里，
        网址会体现在文章目录名中。
      </li>
      <li>扩展不加载远程代码：全部逻辑都打包在扩展内部。</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>如何删除数据</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        在设置页清空各字段可移除保存的配置；卸载扩展则会删除全部本地数据，
        包括剪藏记录。
      </li>
      <li>在 GitHub 的设置中撤销该令牌，即可立即失效。</li>
      <li>剪藏的文章保存在你自己的仓库里，由你自行删除。</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>本站点</h3>
    <p>
      站点是纯静态页面，不设置追踪
      Cookie，不运行分析脚本；搜索完全在浏览器本地完成。
      深色模式偏好保存在浏览器的 <code>localStorage</code> 里。站点托管在 Cloudflare
      Pages，由其按常规方式处理访问日志。
    </p>

    <h2>English</h2>

    <p>
      Tiro is two things: the <strong>Tiro Clipper</strong> Chrome extension and this
      site. Neither sets tracking cookies, runs analytics or ads, and nothing is sold.
      The extension sends data to exactly one third party — GitHub — into the repository
      you name, with your own token, and only after you press Clip.
    </p>

    <h3>What the extension stores</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The GitHub owner, repository, branch, and personal access token (PAT)
        you enter on its options page.
      </li>
      <li>
        These live in <code>chrome.storage.local</code> on that machine only. They
        are not synced across devices and are not uploaded to any server other than
        GitHub.
      </li>
      <li>A record of when you accepted the first-run disclosure.</li>
      <li>Your UI language choice (auto / English / 中文).</li>
      <li>
        A local record of your clips: after each successful clip, the identifier
        (slug) derived from the page's address and the time, used to show an
        "already clipped" status the next time the popup opens on that page. It
        also lives only in <code>chrome.storage.local</code> (at most 500 entries)
        and is never sent anywhere.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>When it reads a page</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When you click the Tiro toolbar icon on a page and the popup opens, the
        extension reads that page to build the preview (title, word count).
        <strong>This happens before you click Clip.</strong>
      </li>
      <li>
        The first time you use it, the popup shows this disclosure and reads
        nothing until you agree to it.
      </li>
      <li>
        The result stays in the browser. Close the popup without clipping and it
        is discarded — not sent, not stored.
      </li>
      <li>
        The extension never reads or uploads pages in the background, and cannot
        touch a page you have not opened the popup on.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What it sends, and where</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The only network destination is <code>https://api.github.com</code>,
        which is also the only entry in the extension's
        <code>host_permissions</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        When you click Clip, it commits to your own repository, with your own
        token: the article as Markdown, its title, the source URL, the domain,
        and the time you clipped it. The title also appears in the commit
        message, and the URL is reflected in the article's directory name.
      </li>
      <li>No remote code is loaded; all logic is bundled in the extension.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Deleting your data</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Clear the fields on the options page to remove the stored settings;
        uninstalling the extension deletes all local data, including the clip
        record.
      </li>
      <li>
        Revoke the token in your GitHub settings to cut off access at once.
      </li>
      <li>Clipped articles live in your own repository; delete them there.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>This site</h3>
    <p>
      The site is static. It sets no tracking cookies and runs no analytics;
      search runs entirely in your browser. Your dark-mode preference is kept in
      <code>localStorage</code>. It is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which handles
      request logs in the ordinary way.
    </p>

    <h3>Contact</h3>
    <p>
      Questions or requests: <a href="https://github.com/hutusi/tiro/issues"
        >github.com/hutusi/tiro/issues</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
